{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1222391-not-necromancy-but-solars-raising-the-dead","id":1222391,"title":"Not Necromancy, but Solars raising the dead","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-27T06:14:34-07:00","id":1222391,"title":"Not Necromancy, but Solars raising the dead","content":"I am trying to write a game to play soon, just need to find the time, but an idea hit me and I wanted to share it. As Abyssals gain strength from the simple act of bloody combat, at the least corpses are left and ghosts rise. What if, a Solar could bind the life of a fallen person to their body? Think of it as a rally to stay alive till the job is done. I haven't read through all of 3Ed to see all new stuff so I may stick to 2Ed. But, I want to see what others thought about this idea, whether this would be a charm, spell or even an artifact. I can see a field of freshly fallen soldiers rising to complete their Lords edicts and burning in a Holy fire at the conclusion.<br /> <br /> I would really like to see if others see this as an interesting story tool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i712.photobucket.com/albums/ww125/PaulJustus/FireAspectink_zpsf63a29e6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />My <a href=\"http://layton224.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">DA</a> page","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2926-layton224","name":"layton224","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2926_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-27T07:08:40-07:00","id":1222400,"title":"","content":"*hums* From a lore perspective, it's a touch borderline, but I'd be okay with it. It's not so much raising the dead as holding them together for one final stand, binding their souls to the bodies through Solar fire. Mechanically I think there's room for it too: a Simple War Charm to create a Rally for Numbers action that<i> isn't </i>capped by the unit's current size. That's not bringing back everyone, but it could be a big swing, especially if you added some kinda rider to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-27T08:02:53-07:00","id":1222418,"title":"","content":"A War charm is a good idea, I think the raised soldiers having a need for an intimacy to the Solar as a Leader (Positive) would be a nice limiting and sensible story hook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i712.photobucket.com/albums/ww125/PaulJustus/FireAspectink_zpsf63a29e6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />My <a href=\"http://layton224.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">DA</a> page","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2926-layton224","name":"layton224","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2926_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-27T08:26:01-07:00","id":1222428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>layton224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1222391-not-necromancy-but-solars-raising-the-dead?p=1222418#post1222418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A War charm is a good idea, I think the raised soldiers having a need for an intimacy to the Solar as a Leader (Positive) would be a nice limiting and sensible story hook.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is already a War Charm with a very similar effect, March of the Returner, I see what you describe as a Stunt for that Charm. Did you know about it? Is here anything mechanical or narrative that you think could be different for it?<br /> <br /> The next Charm, Supremacy of the Divine Army, can call animals and spirits to join your ranks... I'm not getting any ideas immediately on how to differentiate what you say fro March of the Returner in a significant enough way to create a new Charm.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-27T08:45:42-07:00","id":1222431,"title":"","content":"There are dozen of ways to do this, Evocations from soulsteel artifacts, sorcerous workings,..etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-27T08:52:42-07:00","id":1222434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1222391-not-necromancy-but-solars-raising-the-dead?p=1222428#post1222428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is already a War Charm with a very similar effect, March of the Returner, I see what you describe as a Stunt for that Charm. Did you know about it? Is here anything mechanical or narrative that you think could be different for it?<br /> <br /> The next Charm, Supremacy of the Divine Army, can call animals and spirits to join your ranks... I'm not getting any ideas immediately on how to differentiate what you say fro March of the Returner in a significant enough way to create a new Charm.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Is &quot; March of the Returner&quot; a 3Ed charm I am not familiar with it... what book would I reference it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i712.photobucket.com/albums/ww125/PaulJustus/FireAspectink_zpsf63a29e6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />My <a href=\"http://layton224.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">DA</a> page","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2926-layton224","name":"layton224","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2926_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-27T08:55:10-07:00","id":1222436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>layton224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1222391-not-necromancy-but-solars-raising-the-dead?p=1222434#post1222434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Is &quot; March of the Returner&quot; a 3Ed charm I am not familiar with it... what book would I reference it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it is from the 3e Core page 423<br /> <br /> &quot;The Solar represents a new dawn on the last day of Creation.<br /> Her coming foretells the battle\u2019s end, a day of blood for the<br /> wicked and light to vanquish darkness from the world once<br /> more. When her army is routed, the Lawgiver may call upon<br /> glories past\u2014in this life and those that came before\u2014to create<br /> a rallying tactic that miraculously reforms her army. This<br /> Charm is an automatically successful rally action (p. 210).<br /> It can be used once per scene, but it can be reset if the Solar<br /> succeeds at vanquishing a terrible foe or conquering a powerful<br /> enemy through the might of her army.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-27T09:04:16-07:00","id":1222437,"title":"","content":"Ok, thanks... I was able to find it after I posted. I see this as very similar as well. I need to find time to read the third edition, lol.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i712.photobucket.com/albums/ww125/PaulJustus/FireAspectink_zpsf63a29e6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />My <a href=\"http://layton224.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">DA</a> page","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2926-layton224","name":"layton224","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2926_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-27T17:25:45-07:00","id":1222550,"title":"","content":"In the game I ran, the Twilight had a guilty conscience after her Limit Break resulted in significant casualties among the Dawn's mercenary company. We were spitballing sorcerous workings she might undertake to make up for it, and one of the ideas was:<br /> <br /> Unblinking Vanguard of the Sun would be an Ambition 2 Celestial working that safeguards the lives of the affected battle group. Searing heat automatically cauterizes wounds, blinding flashes interrupt deathblows, and if the unit is completely shattered, the spirits of the fallen tarry upon the battlefield as ghostly legionnaires of living sunlight to negate the defense penalty suffered during slaughter actions.<br /> <br /> Save for the last bit, it largely served limit losses suffered after battle, which is not something comprehensively represented, mechanically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2223-ketrus","name":"Ketrus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"398"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-27T17:53:59-07:00","id":1222553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>layton224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1222391-not-necromancy-but-solars-raising-the-dead?p=1222437#post1222437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, thanks... I was able to find it after I posted. I see this as very similar as well. I need to find time to read the third edition, lol.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yah, it has awesome stuff!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ketrus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1222391-not-necromancy-but-solars-raising-the-dead?p=1222550#post1222550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the game I ran, the Twilight had a guilty conscience after her Limit Break resulted in significant casualties among the Dawn's mercenary company. We were spitballing sorcerous workings she might undertake to make up for it, and one of the ideas was:<br /> <br /> Unblinking Vanguard of the Sun would be an Ambition 2 Celestial working that safeguards the lives of the affected battle group. Searing heat automatically cauterizes wounds, blinding flashes interrupt deathblows, and if the unit is completely shattered, the spirits of the fallen tarry upon the battlefield as ghostly legionnaires of living sunlight to negate the defense penalty suffered during slaughter actions.<br /> <br /> Save for the last bit, it largely served limit losses suffered after battle, which is not something comprehensively represented, mechanically.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats a cool idea!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-27T18:13:56-07:00","id":1222558,"title":"","content":"I do wonder at the idea of a Charm to rally the dying or only mostly dead when the system doesn't exactly represent those in mechanics very precisely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-27T18:35:21-07:00","id":1222560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1222391-not-necromancy-but-solars-raising-the-dead?p=1222558#post1222558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do wonder at the idea of a Charm to rally the dying or only mostly dead when the system doesn't exactly represent those in mechanics very precisely.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think it falls in that grey area between mechanics-death and narrative-death where reversing death without it having to narratively be a true resurrection is still possible provided you act immediately. There's already a couple of Charms that play around with that grey area a bit and March of the Returner is one of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-27T20:23:49-07:00","id":1222571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>layton224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1222391-not-necromancy-but-solars-raising-the-dead#post1222391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am trying to write a game to play soon, just need to find the time, but an idea hit me and I wanted to share it. As Abyssals gain strength from the simple act of bloody combat, at the least corpses are left and ghosts rise. What if, a Solar could bind the life of a fallen person to their body? Think of it as a rally to stay alive till the job is done. I haven't read through all of 3Ed to see all new stuff so I may stick to 2Ed. But, I want to see what others thought about this idea, whether this would be a charm, spell or even an artifact. I can see a field of freshly fallen soldiers rising to complete their Lords edicts and burning in a Holy fire at the conclusion.<br /> <br /> I would really like to see if others see this as an interesting story tool.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the idea, at least in a dramatic sense. I could see it as a potential capstone charm for a War charm-tree. <br /> <br /> Conceptually I see this as very powerful mojo. Might produce serious balance issues -- imagine a battlegroup that can't be defeated short of complete destruction (disintegration, dismemberment, being irretrievably lost in sea depths, etc).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11847-kfinigan","name":"KFinigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-28T08:48:47-07:00","id":1222663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1222391-not-necromancy-but-solars-raising-the-dead?p=1222560#post1222560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I think it falls in that grey area between mechanics-death and narrative-death where reversing death without it having to narratively be a true resurrection is still possible provided you act immediately. There's already a couple of Charms that play around with that grey area a bit and March of the Returner is one of them.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200bI'm talking more about the fact that damaging a battle group's Magnitude doesn't really precisely track to them being killed, so it creates a question on how to arbitrate when a group falling apart entirely is because they all died rather than because most ran away.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200bSudden idea: the Charm would build off of Tiger Warrior Training Technique and only function on people that had been trained to have perfect morale. It both removes ambiguity from the scenarios in which the Charm can be used (a battle group with perfect morale reduced to nothing can be handily assumed to basically have been killed in its entirety), and creates a stronger thematic basis for the effect both in terms of the troops' bond with their commander, and in the strength of spirit that the Solar is able to kindle to get them to rise up for one last crack at it.<br /> <br /> \u200bMaybe also limited to only being used for troops that fell in pursuit of a Defining Intimacy that is shared with the Solar.</span></span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-28T17:39:56-07:00","id":1222760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1222391-not-necromancy-but-solars-raising-the-dead?p=1222560#post1222560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think it falls in that grey area between mechanics-death and narrative-death where reversing death without it having to narratively be a true resurrection is still possible provided you act immediately. There's already a couple of Charms that play around with that grey area a bit and March of the Returner is one of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, I never thought of March of the Returner working like that, It always seemed to me like it was more about calling back the parts of your army that lost their nerve/started to flee.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Life before Death, Strength before Weakness, Journey before Destination.&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">&quot;I will protect those who cannot protect themselves&quot;</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4172-marros56","name":"Marros56","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4172_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-28T18:57:42-07:00","id":1222779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marros56</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1222391-not-necromancy-but-solars-raising-the-dead?p=1222760#post1222760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Huh, I never thought of March of the Returner working like that, It always seemed to me like it was more about calling back the parts of your army that lost their nerve/started to flee.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s that too, but the degree of restoration would imply some people struck down pulled themselves back up at your call","signatu